# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
#
# TSan suppressions for the nightly `tsan` lane (issue #702, docs/specs/memory-model-v1.md
# section 10).
#
# Format: one entry per line, `interceptor:pattern` (or `race:pattern` for a reported race),
# preceded by a `#` comment line that gives the reason. The sanitizer runtime ignores blank lines and
# `#` comments.
#
# POLICY - read before adding a line:
#   * Tessera's own code is NEVER suppressed here. A race in our code is a bug to fix; the lane
#     exists to surface it.
#   * Only a third-party library may be listed, and only with a reason that names the library, the
#     report it emits and why the report is not ours to fix.
#
# CURRENT STATE: empty. TSan has not been run against this tree yet (issue #702 lists it as still to
# measure), so no suppression is known to be needed. If the first runs report third-party noise, the
# entry goes here with its reason rather than in the workflow.
